    <string name="goal_solver_title">Goal Solver</string>
    <string name="goal_solver_description">Answers: “how much capital do I need TODAY to quit at the given age and never drop below the happiness threshold?”. The answer depends on how much of your surplus you save while working (P1), so it is a TABLE, not a single number: each row is a saving ratio P1 with its minimum capital. In the goal plan you save P1 of the surplus until the stop age (P2 = P4 = stop age) and from then on the plan draws from capital exactly the yearly amount that keeps utility at the threshold (P3 = 0 means: no extra percentage draw — the engine spends the utility minimum from capital). Your capital-to-keep-at-death is still enforced. Select a row and Apply installs that whole plan.</string>
